WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Colibri activates 3.46 billion parameters per token, putting open English German serving on the cost frontier. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 215. A Latin encoder, a Schema coherence inventory, and a critic reused as a confidence estimator follow. Then the engineering tear down. Colibri is a new English German mixture of experts transformer, which routes each token through only a subset of the network, according to the archive report. Total size is 78.1 billion parameters.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.780
Training used 24 trillion tokens and German made up more than 20% of that mix by bytes.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.260
Supervised fine-tuning and reinforcement learning followed.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:45.280
On more than 1.2 million in-house tasks spanning reasoning, tool use, instruction following,

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.640
code and retrieval.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.100
Only 4.4% of the weight's fire for each token.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:56.100
A controlled model factory pipeline handled data curation, training infrastructure, post-training,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:02.020
and evaluation, aimed at sovereign and regulated domain use, and the weights ship under Apache

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:09.238
2.0. Latin now has a modern BERT-based encoder called LAMB, pre-trained in two phases with

00:01:09.238 --> 00:01:11.618
a morphologically informed masking regimen.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:18.518
Mark Tech Post reports pre-training consumed more than 74 billion Latin tokens. LAMB outperforms

00:01:18.518 --> 00:01:26.038
all other evaluated models on 16 of 17 sub-tasks across 5 tasks. It comes within 0.8 percentage

00:01:26.038 --> 00:01:28.678
points of state-of-the-art on the remaining subtask.

00:01:29.098 --> 00:01:33.338
The release includes a service with 24 billion bird-word piece tokens.

00:01:33.938 --> 00:01:39.138
It also includes Corpus Trinum, the first Latin semantic triplet data set, containing

00:01:39.138 --> 00:01:41.698
over 100 million strong and weak triplets.

00:01:42.848 --> 00:01:47.968
Schema Coherence Inventory provides 96 forced choice items in an archive paper.

00:01:48.588 --> 00:01:53.928
Items sit at 8 levels of Beck's cognitive model, a clinical hierarchy of beliefs, and are

00:01:53.928 --> 00:01:58.968
scored by length normalized log likelihood, a probability score that needs no generation

00:01:58.968 --> 00:01:59.828
or parsing.

00:02:00.368 --> 00:02:07.368
Six validation studies ran across 107 conditions on 5 backbones from 1.7 billion to 14 billion

00:02:07.368 --> 00:02:07.928
parameters.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:14.288
Belief adapters prove target specific on every backbone, with a gain of 17.7 points.

00:02:14.848 --> 00:02:20.128
A conditions inventory profile identifies its own free generations in 24 of 30 cases,

00:02:20.568 --> 00:02:22.248
against 5 expected by chance.

00:02:22.248 --> 00:02:27.988
9 clinically trained Raiders recover the keyed belief at 79.5% accuracy.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:34.660
Free lunch for LLM's confidence shows an external model trained only on a policy's behavioral traces

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:41.640
can estimate that policy's confidence as accurately as the policy itself, without accessing internal representations.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:47.860
Under a correctness-based outcome, confidence estimation and critic training are mathematically equivalent.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:52.140
Both predicting from a trajectory how likely a response is to be correct.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:57.840
The reused critic is the best confidence estimator on every indistribution split, and the

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:04.240
best calibrated on 14 of 16 splits across math, code, tool calling, and general reasoning

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.220
without hurting task performance.

00:03:07.385 --> 00:03:13.845
Specmem maintains a live per user tool call memory with least recently used, or LRU, eviction,

00:03:13.845 --> 00:03:17.965
and a side-effect gate that defers irreversible calls until verification.

00:03:18.805 --> 00:03:23.785
Oblations show the gain comes almost entirely from keeping the store live, rather than from

00:03:23.785 --> 00:03:25.285
local per-user scoping.

00:03:26.252 --> 00:03:31.372
Modality-specific perception agents post-evident sighted observations to a shared board for

00:03:31.372 --> 00:03:33.052
conversational emotion reasoning.

00:03:33.432 --> 00:03:39.352
An integration agent produces an emotion description and label set with citations, and a multimodal

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:42.192
large-language model critic can request one revision.

00:03:42.192 --> 00:03:49.612
On the Mayr 2025 data set, F-score rose between 0.6 and 2.2 points depending on the backbone

00:03:49.612 --> 00:04:00.332
across Video Lama 32B, 5.3.5 Vision Instruct, Quen 2.5 VL7B Instruct, and interned VL 2.538B.

00:04:00.832 --> 00:04:05.692
The pipeline beat both a frozen static setup and undifferentiated reflection baselines.

00:04:05.692 --> 00:04:11.867
Solo.io introduced agent shield to protect existing infrastructure from AI agents and

00:04:11.867 --> 00:04:15.187
organization does not control, AI Authority reports.

00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:20.147
The tool targets security and governance gaps that appear when those outside agents touch

00:04:20.147 --> 00:04:21.207
internal systems.

00:04:22.171 --> 00:04:27.791
Singhua released AKV as an SG-Lang-based cash engineering server, according to Mark Tech

00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:28.211
Post.

00:04:28.851 --> 00:04:33.991
LLM agents can drop and reposition key value cash rather than summarizing prior turns.

00:04:33.991 --> 00:04:40.491
Average costs fell 27.7% across four-age and benchmarks, with performance preserved.

00:04:41.537 --> 00:04:46.777
LLNs runs inside the closed network of Hokkaido University Hospital, using the open-weight

00:04:46.777 --> 00:04:50.037
Kemi-K 2.6 model in an archive study.

00:04:50.557 --> 00:04:54.637
The stack sits on one host with 8 NVIDIA H200 GPUs.

00:04:55.077 --> 00:05:01.957
On 180 questions over hospital documents, it reaches 97.2% mean accuracy, with interactive

00:05:01.957 --> 00:05:03.217
document tool access.

00:05:03.217 --> 00:05:10.477
that is 15.9% points above fixed retrieval, with the largest gains on filtering and counting questions.

00:05:11.459 --> 00:05:19.319
X-Dubbing jointly solves time-aware speech-to-text translation and video-aware text-to-speech using a language-agnostic timing budget.

00:05:19.799 --> 00:05:24.099
It produces faithful translations that remain naturally speakable within source timing.

00:05:24.099 --> 00:05:29.939
ISO crony, meaning the speech still fits the original timing, and audio-visual correspondence

00:05:29.939 --> 00:05:34.879
both improve over recent baselines, and the system does not need paired dubbing data.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:41.250
Misconcept dialogue ran five open-weight LLM tutors against LLM simulated students.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.970
The run covered over 5,000 dialogues.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:50.830
Benchmark style exact match scoring reports 42.1% remediation success on the same dialogues

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.510
where a human-calibrated LLM as judge reports 81.3%.

00:05:55.510 --> 00:06:00.870
That 39.2 percentage point spread is larger than the combined effects of tutor model,

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.230
teaching strategy, and supply diagnostic information.

00:06:05.222 --> 00:06:10.282
Graph-based reasoning recasts structured generation as an ambiguity-aware inference problem

00:06:10.282 --> 00:06:15.342
that reasons over a set of plausible structured outputs rather than predicting a single solution.

00:06:15.342 --> 00:06:21.502
Reasoning over semantic alignment and relational consistency improves accuracy, stability and

00:06:21.502 --> 00:06:25.802
robustness under varying levels of ambiguity on structured generation benchmarks.

00:06:26.727 --> 00:06:32.087
River decomposes agent outputs into atomic claims and tracks convergence, exploration,

00:06:32.487 --> 00:06:32.987
and retention.

00:06:33.687 --> 00:06:38.127
Tess used five interaction strategies on 40 controlled news generation cases.

00:06:38.687 --> 00:06:43.627
Repeatedly pooled interaction promotes convergence but narrows the information space, while

00:06:43.627 --> 00:06:46.747
distributed relay yields broader, less-shared information.

00:06:47.805 --> 00:06:51.745
SCI agent exam benchmarks agents on scientific research tasks.

00:06:52.205 --> 00:06:59.045
It comprises 120 expert curated tasks across 11 scientific fields and 7 research task types.

00:06:59.645 --> 00:07:03.685
GPT-6 Astra achieves the highest overall score of 80.9.

00:07:04.225 --> 00:07:09.165
Only 26.0% of its runs exceed the 0.95 success threshold.

00:07:09.165 --> 00:07:15.305
The results revealed distinct capability profiles and variation in execution efficiency and stability.

00:07:16.248 --> 00:07:22.168
In brief, an audit of 288 responses posted an overall F1 of 0.916,

00:07:22.788 --> 00:07:28.008
yet prompt specific score errors ran from 2.6% to 33.3%,

00:07:28.008 --> 00:07:34.028
and a 9.3 point lift from asserting certainty shrank to 2.3 points once both raiders scored it.

00:07:34.028 --> 00:07:39.748
Corpse Dial builds pre-consultation dialogues with a persona-driven patient agent and a

00:07:39.748 --> 00:07:45.948
process-guided doctor agent, then applies post-talk checks for role-consistency, workflow-completeness

00:07:45.948 --> 00:07:51.748
and textual consistency, lifting alignment with real dialogues on coverage, clinical compliance

00:07:51.748 --> 00:07:52.768
and naturalness.

00:07:53.288 --> 00:07:58.768
ProfileSim jointly models user demographics, big five personality traits, and business

00:07:58.768 --> 00:08:03.848
intents reverse engineered from real call logs, then refines that base with group relative

00:08:03.848 --> 00:08:07.128
of policy optimization under hierarchical dialogue level

00:08:07.128 --> 00:08:08.588
and utterance level rewards.

00:08:09.691 --> 00:08:11.471
Deploy the open weights of Colibri

00:08:11.471 --> 00:08:13.191
if you need English German performance

00:08:13.191 --> 00:08:15.351
and full control over data residency.

00:08:15.931 --> 00:08:18.071
Run the Schema coherence inventory items

00:08:18.071 --> 00:08:20.511
against any persona-conditioned model you use

00:08:20.511 --> 00:08:22.791
for simulated patients or effective agents

00:08:23.061 --> 00:08:26.171
to check whether assigned beliefs actually organize behavior.

00:08:26.731 --> 00:08:29.651
Try AKV on SGLANG-based agent workloads

00:08:29.651 --> 00:08:31.711
where history summarization is currently

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:33.071
the dominant cost driver.

00:08:33.071 --> 00:08:39.915
Score a sample of tutor dialogues with both exact match and a human calibrated judge, and look at the gap.

00:08:40.415 --> 00:08:46.295
More open-weight mixture of experts releases are expected to target the 3-4 billion active parameter regime.

00:08:46.955 --> 00:08:52.595
Additional agent memory frameworks will likely adopt live per user stores with explicit side-effect gating.

00:08:53.565 --> 00:09:01.245
Frozen draft stores start going stale the moment user behavior drifts, so let's pop the hood on speculative decoding with live per user memory.

00:09:01.245 --> 00:09:07.205
Speculative decoding already reuses past token sequences as drafts, which is how a model

00:09:07.205 --> 00:09:09.985
guesses several tokens ahead and then verifies them.

00:09:10.585 --> 00:09:15.565
Most deployments freeze that draft store at build time, so acceptance rates decay as each

00:09:15.565 --> 00:09:17.405
user's tool calling habits change.

00:09:18.145 --> 00:09:23.045
Speck Mem writes every verified tool call back into a bounded per user least recently

00:09:23.045 --> 00:09:25.045
used store during live operation.

00:09:25.745 --> 00:09:29.885
The memory becomes a continuously updated cache of that user's recurring patterns.

00:09:29.885 --> 00:09:35.065
A side effect gate runs a deterministic check before any irreversible action is allowed

00:09:35.065 --> 00:09:35.785
to be drafted.

00:09:36.365 --> 00:09:40.765
That removes the failure mode where a high confidence but dangerous call slips through

00:09:40.765 --> 00:09:41.845
on a stale draft.

00:09:42.365 --> 00:09:48.065
Because the store is scoped per user, cross-user leakage disappears without extra isolation layers.

00:09:48.605 --> 00:09:53.765
On multi-session, multi-user query streams served by three open-weight models, it holds

00:09:53.765 --> 00:09:59.345
a 27% gap in mean-accepted tokens against a frozen store that steadily loses acceptance.

00:09:59.345 --> 00:10:06.165
While clock speed up reaches 1.74 times, because fewer tokens are decoded auto-regressively

00:10:06.165 --> 00:10:11.265
once the store stabilizes, the tradeoff is extra memory per active user and the need

00:10:11.265 --> 00:10:13.105
to persist the store across sessions.

00:10:13.645 --> 00:10:18.265
Forgetting to gate irreversible actions turns the optimization into a correctness regression.

00:10:18.925 --> 00:10:23.605
Teams should adopt live memory when they already log tool calls and can afford per user

00:10:23.605 --> 00:10:29.165
state, and otherwise a static high-quality seed store plus periodic refresh remains simpler.

00:10:30.081 --> 00:10:35.001
Before we go, the next interactive evaluation paper may lead with per prompt score error

00:10:35.621 --> 00:10:37.681
rather than one overall accuracy number.

